  "solution": {
    "text": "<math><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></mrow></mfenced></math> Option <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></mfenced></math> is true only if <math><mi>p</mi></math> is true and <math><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mo>&#8764;</mo><mi>p</mi><mo>&#8658;</mo><mo>&#8764;</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></mfenced></math> is false which can never be possible, hence <math><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></mrow></mfenced></math> is a fallacy<br /><math><mo>&#8756;</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo><mi>t</mi></math> is a tautology, if <math><mi>s</mi></math> is subset of <math><mi>t</mi></math><br /><math><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi></mrow></mfenced></math> <math><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>&#8743;</mo><mo>&#8764;</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></mfenced></math> is a subset of <math><mi>p,</mi></math> hence <math><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>&#8743;</mo><mo>&#8764;</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>p</mi></math> is a tautology, hence <math><mo>&#8764;</mo><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>&#8743;</mo><mo>&#8764;</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></mfenced></math> is a fallacy<br /><math><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></mrow></mfenced></math> <math><mi>p</mi></math> is a subset of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>&#8744;</mo><mo>~</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></mfenced></math>, hence <math><mi>p</mi><mo>&#8658;</mo><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>&#8744;</mo><mo>&#8764;</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></mfenced></math> is a tautology, hence <math><mo>&#8764;</mo><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>&#8658;</mo><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>&#8744;</mo><mo>&#8764;</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></mfenced></mrow></mfenced></math> is a fallacy<br /><math><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">D</mi></mrow></mfenced></math> Option <math><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">D</mi></mrow></mfenced></math> is the negation of option <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mi>A</mi></mfenced></math>, hence <math><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">D</mi></mrow></mfenced></math> is a tautology"
